{
  "_doc": [
    "Shared by the capture script (writes raw/) and scripts/screenshots/frame.mjs (writes appstore/<App Store language>/).",
    "Capture needs only: iphone[].id + iphone[].theme -> raw/<lang>/iphone/<theme>/<id>.png at 1320x2868,",
    "and watch[].id -> raw/<lang>/watch/<id>.png at the Ultra 3 native size (422x514).",
    "The same iphone[] list is rendered again for the iPad from raw/<lang>/ipad/<theme>/<id>.png (2064x2752);",
    "a layout of phone-watch is iPhone-only, so that slide is left out of the iPad set, number and all.",
    "Framing fields: title, subtitle, note (small closing line) — each a message KEY, not text: the words live in packages/i18n/locales/<lang>/store.json (\\n = manual break) and reach frame.mjs as screenshots/i18n/<lang>.json via `bun run i18n`;",
    "layout = phone | phone-bottom | phone-watch, watch = <watch id> to compose beside the phone,",
    "bg = slide background (text colour is derived from its luminance), accent = rule colour.",
    "Devices are composited into Apple's own product bezels from screenshots/frames/.",
    "iphone[] is the numbered App Store set, in order; max 10.",
    "extras[] uses the same schema but renders to appstore/<lang>/extras/ instead: unnumbered spares,",
    "kept out of the contact sheet unless you pass --contact-sheet=all. Promote one by moving it",
    "into iphone[] (and dropping one of the ten)."
  ],
